   "text": {
    "L1": "Data can answer questions about counts and measurements.",
    "L2": "But data does not automatically prove every claim. That is our myth to bust.",
    "L3": "Use the numbers the statement talks about, and find them in the table.",
    "L4": "For this statement, July is 250 millimetres. June and September together are 140 plus 120, or 260.",
    "L5": "Now compare 250 with 260. Since 250 is less than 260, the statement is false.",
    "L6": "A statement checked against data can be true, false, or cannot tell from this data.",
    "L7": "Also, two things rising together does not prove that one causes the other.",
    "L8": "And one case or a tiny sample is not enough to claim something about everyone."
   },
